    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the whole build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature so that `POST /api/owners` accepts an optional `title` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns a composed `salutation`.\n\n**Spec behavior:** `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is supplied, otherwise just `lastName`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR`) to the editable `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only derived `salutation` field to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs are code-generated from this spec.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a `title` column with getter/setter, so the value persists between the create and the later read.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", ...)` backed by a `salutation(owner)` helper that composes the string (treating null/blank title as \"no title\"). MapStruct maps the `title` enum\u2194`String` automatically (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`).\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table (tests run against hsqldb where `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the schema; updated the other dialects for consistency).\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
